---
import { journey } from "../../data/journey";

const ask = journey.flatMap((stage) => stage.modules).find((m) => m.slug === "01-collection")!.ask;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/, "/");
const film = (name: string) => `${base}film/${name}`;
const next = [
  ["../01-collection-field-work/?from=carry-it#assistant", "Test your own assistant", "on the pages Kick got, with a gap nothing mentions"],
  ["../01-collection-field-work/?from=carry-it#statistics", "Statistics of the gap", "missingness mechanisms, and bounds that depend on each other"],
  ["../01-collection-field-work/?from=carry-it#platform", "How Touchline builds it", "merge, atomic write and reruns"],
  ["../01-collection-field-work/?from=carry-it#lab", "The lab", "write Friday's coverage record in Python"],
];
---

<section id="carry-it">
  <h2>Carry it: the same number, twice</h2>
  <p>A health network has ten clinics that report patient visits each week. For week 9 you hold the same spreadsheet in two worlds: eight rows, sum 100.</p>
  <div class="cv-twins">
    <div>
      <h3>World A</h3>
      <p>The other two clinics each sent a file with a header and no rows. Both were closed that week for refitting, and the closure notices are on file.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>World B</h3>
      <p>The other two sent nothing. Nobody has heard from them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cv-commit" data-commit>
    <label class="cv-write" for="cv-a">World A headline</label>
    <textarea id="cv-a" rows="2" data-save="transfer-a"></textarea>
    <label class="cv-write" for="cv-b">World B headline</label>
    <textarea id="cv-b" rows="2" data-save="transfer-b"></textarea>
    <button type="button" disabled>Compare with worked answers</button>
    <p class="cv-once" data-needs-note>Write a full sentence in each box to compare.</p>
    <div class="cv-reveal">
      <p class="cv-model">A: 100 visits across all ten clinics. Two were closed.</p>
      <p class="cv-model">B: At least 100 visits, from eight of ten clinics. Two have not reported.</p>
      <p>World A's two clinics are <em>empty</em>: they answered, the answer is proved, and it is zero. World B's are <em>unavailable</em>. The number 100 is a total in A and a lower bound in B.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>The one ask</h3>
  <p>Take this to any AI that collects anything for you.</p>
  <div class="cv-prompt">
    <p data-copy-text>{ask}</p>
    <button type="button" data-copy data-label="Copy the ask">Copy the ask</button>
  </div>

  <h3>Then Tuesday</h3>
  <p>Two minutes to close the module: what the three calls taught, and the bug that opens the next one.</p>
  <figure class="cv-film">
    <video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster={film("monday-then-tuesday.jpg")} aria-label="Monday, Then Tuesday, a two-minute closing film for Module 1">
      <source src={film("monday-then-tuesday.mp4")} type="video/mp4" />
      <track kind="captions" src={film("monday-then-tuesday.vtt")} srclang="en" label="English" default />
    </video>
    <figcaption>Monday, Then Tuesday. Every count on screen is the sample's.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p class="cv-next">Riley's question is where Module 2 starts. <a href="../02-archive/">Module 2: The raw archive</a></p>

  <h3>Go further first</h3>
  <p>Each of these is optional and stands alone, on the <a href="../01-collection-field-work/?from=carry-it">field work page</a>.</p>
  <ul class="cv-next-links">
    {next.map(([href, name, what]) => <li><a href={href}>{name}</a><span>{what}</span></li>)}
  </ul>
  <button type="button" class="cv-quiet" data-reset>Clear my answers and start this module again</button>
</section>
